WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.455
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.755 --> 00:00:08.979
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.279 --> 00:00:14.868
Unit two: Present Continuous. Today you will describe actions happening now.

4
00:00:15.168 --> 00:00:17.867
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:22.333
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.183 --> 00:00:23.975
Now.

7
00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:26.809
Now means at this moment.

8
00:00:27.417 --> 00:00:28.638
I am working now.

9
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.821
Your turn. Say: Now.

10
00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:35.575
Now.

11
00:00:36.317 --> 00:00:37.271
Right now.

12
00:00:38.283 --> 00:00:40.852
Right now means exactly at this moment.

13
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:43.078
She is sleeping right now.

14
00:00:43.683 --> 00:00:46.138
Your turn. Say: Right now.

15
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.106
Right now.

16
00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:51.886
Am doing.

17
00:00:52.883 --> 00:00:55.266
Am doing means I am in the middle of doing it.

18
00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:57.315
I am doing my homework.

19
00:00:57.917 --> 00:01:00.209
Your turn. Say: Am doing.

20
00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:04.149
Am doing.

21
00:01:04.883 --> 00:01:05.826
Is doing.

22
00:01:06.817 --> 00:01:10.314
Is doing means he, she or it is in the middle of doing it.

23
00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:12.626
He is doing his job.

24
00:01:13.217 --> 00:01:15.347
Your turn. Say: Is doing.

25
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.073
Is doing.

26
00:01:19.817 --> 00:01:20.806
Are doing.

27
00:01:21.817 --> 00:01:24.548
Are doing means you, we or they are in the middle of doing it.

28
00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:26.906
They are doing exercises.

29
00:01:27.517 --> 00:01:29.809
Your turn. Say: Are doing.

30
00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:33.528
Are doing.

31
00:01:34.283 --> 00:01:35.133
Currently.

32
00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.254
Currently means at the present time.

33
00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:40.478
She is currently studying.

34
00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:43.562
Your turn. Say: Currently.

35
00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.366
Currently.

36
00:01:48.117 --> 00:01:48.990
Action.

37
00:01:49.983 --> 00:01:52.389
Action means something that someone does.

38
00:01:52.983 --> 00:01:54.356
Running is an action.

39
00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:57.138
Your turn. Say: Action.

40
00:01:60.000 --> 00:02:00.931
Action.

41
00:02:01.683 --> 00:02:02.499
Happening.

42
00:02:03.483 --> 00:02:05.587
Happening means taking place now.

43
00:02:06.183 --> 00:02:08.078
Something is happening outside.

44
00:02:08.683 --> 00:02:11.011
Your turn. Say: Happening.

45
00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:14.763
Happening.

46
00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:19.159
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:20.017 --> 00:02:22.341
Visal, what are you doing right now?

48
00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:34.044
I am talking to you. We use am, is or are with the -ing form for actions happening now: I am talking, she is working, they are playing.

49
00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:36.743
Can we use it for the future?

50
00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:48.211
Yes, for fixed plans: I am meeting my friend tomorrow. But today we focus on now and around now: She is currently studying English.

51
00:02:49.317 --> 00:02:51.212
Which verbs do not use it?

52
00:02:52.317 --> 00:03:02.924
State verbs such as know, like, want and love. We say I know the answer, not I am knowing. Remember to double the last consonant: run, running; sit, sitting.

53
00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:05.776
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:06.617 --> 00:03:11.693
Grammar focus: Present continuous: am and is and are plus verb-ing.

55
00:03:11.993 --> 00:03:13.122
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:13.817 --> 00:03:15.491
I am doing my homework now.

57
00:03:16.383 --> 00:03:18.476
She is currently studying English.

58
00:03:19.383 --> 00:03:21.220
They are playing outside right now.

59
00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:29.161
Use am / is / are + verb-ing for actions happening now or around now. Do not use it with state verbs such as know, like and want.

60
00:03:29.917 --> 00:03:33.184
Be careful! Don't say: I am knowing the answer.

61
00:03:35.133 --> 00:03:37.040
Say: I know the answer.

62
00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:39.398
Do not use know in the continuous.

63
00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.945
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:43.733 --> 00:03:44.827
What Is Happening?.

65
00:03:45.127 --> 00:03:48.717
Right now I am sitting at my desk and I am studying English.

66
00:03:49.733 --> 00:03:52.046
My sister is cooking dinner in the kitchen.

67
00:03:53.033 --> 00:03:55.242
My parents are watching the news.

68
00:03:56.233 --> 00:03:59.417
Currently, it is raining, so nobody is playing outside.

69
00:04:00.433 --> 00:04:03.269
Something interesting is always happening around us.

70
00:04:04.367 --> 00:04:08.519
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:09.383 --> 00:04:10.849
She blank a letter now.

72
00:04:11.149 --> 00:04:14.419
A, writes. B, is writing. C, write.

73
00:04:17.967 --> 00:04:19.827
The answer is B: is writing.

74
00:04:20.983 --> 00:04:22.890
They blank football at the moment.

75
00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:26.692
A, are playing. B, is playing. C, plays.

76
00:04:30.233 --> 00:04:32.570
The answer is A: are playing.

77
00:04:33.717 --> 00:04:36.343
Which verb is not used in the continuous?

78
00:04:36.643 --> 00:04:39.205
A, run. B, know. C, eat.

79
00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:44.441
The answer is B: know.

80
00:04:45.583 --> 00:04:47.211
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:47.511 --> 00:04:52.628
A, I am knowing the answer.. B, I know the answer.. C, I knowing the answer..

82
00:04:56.167 --> 00:04:58.979
The answer is B: I know the answer..

83
00:05:00.117 --> 00:05:02.395
According to the reading, who is cooking dinner?

84
00:05:02.695 --> 00:05:06.743
A, my sister. B, my parents. C, the writer.

85
00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.369
The answer is A: my sister.

86
00:05:13.567 --> 00:05:16.962
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:19.201
What are you doing right now?

88
00:05:28.017 --> 00:05:29.412
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:29.712 --> 00:05:42.166
Right now I am sitting at my desk and answering your question. My teacher is listening and my classmates are writing. I use the present continuous because the action is happening at this moment.

90
00:05:42.466 --> 00:05:44.210
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:45.117 --> 00:05:51.612
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present continuous: am and is and are plus verb-ing.

92
00:05:51.912 --> 00:05:55.400
Today's value is attention. Look carefully and listen well.

93
00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:58.144
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

94
00:05:58.444 --> 00:06:01.363
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

